speechtext:
1.	Since 1918 what statutory revisions have been made by the federal government in (a) pay and allowances of military officers of at least field rank or their equivalent; (b) retirement pensions for the above; (c) pay and allowances of privates or equivalent and retirement pensions;
2.	Pay and allowances and retirement pensions for (a) commissioner; (b) constable of the R.C.M.P.;
3.	Pay and allowances of ministers of the crown and members of parliament;
4.	Pay and allowances of supreme court judges and retirement pensions;
5.	Pay and allowances of trade commissioners and senior diplomats and retirement pensions;
6.	Pay and allowances for civil service commissioners and retirement pensions;
7.	Pay and allowances of deputy ministers and retirement pensions;
8.	Pay and allowances of class 1 clerks and retirement pensions;
9.	Federal old age pension contributions;
10.	Recipients of war veterans' allowances;
11.	Disability pension payments for 100 per cent active service pensioners and/or 'their dependents?
